RECORDED – 9.0.10 download of a queue file INUBIT does not have, in an existing workflow
(exit 0, neutralized). INUBIT answers both parts with the exception chain
java.lang.RuntimeException>com.inubit.ibis.utils.InubitException and a two-line message
"Exception from service object: @Start@Unable to download@@@Unable to download@End@<path>",
the path naming owner, workflow, state and file (.wfsp for the variables), as on 8.1.17.
Expected: the marker "@Start@Unable to download" classifies both parts NotFound.

Frames use the fixed nonce 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef; a replay replaces it with the
nonce of its request. Lines without the frame prefix are vendor noise the classifier ignores
(one recorded warning of the helper's network library).
Used by QueueEntryHelperClassifierTest and QueueEntryV90ContractTest (tasks.md T019, T037, T038,
research D-5, D-18, D-21).
